  "prefLabel": "Rev 1906.01 Bonds and Notes Register",
  "priorExpiration": "1998-03-16",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 1906.01 Bonds and Notes Register.\n\n(a) Municipal treasurers shall maintain a record of bonds and notes issued by the municipality, pursuant to RSA 33:12, in the form of a bond and note register.\n\n(b) In addition to the requirements stated in RSA 33:12, the register shall include the following information:\n\n(1) The name of the bank certifying the note or bond;\n\n(2) The date the note or bond was authorized by the legislative body;\n\n(3) The price for which each note or bond was sold, and the name of the purchaser of the note or bond;\n\n(4) The rate of interest;\n\n(5) Title of the municipal official signing the note or bond issue; and\n\n(6) The date and amount of payment of principal and interest.\n\nSource. #5356, eff 3-16-92, EXPIRED: 3-16-98\n\nNew. #6732, eff 4-18-98; ss by #8599, eff 4-6-06; ss by #10582, eff 5-2-14; ss by #13918, eff 3-29-24 (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Rev 1900)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev1900.html"
